; calldata_hole_reads_as_unset: reading a slot the host left unset leaves
; the register unset rather than storing a null in it.
;
; The slot is in range, so INPUT does not fault -- spec/xqvm/ISA.md's INPUT
; row reserves CallDataIndex for a slot outside [0, slots). What it copies
; is the entry's unset-ness: exec_input clones RegVal::Unset into the
; register, so LOAD then raises UnsetRegister.
;
; xqvm_py stored None in the register instead, which no opcode accepts, so
; the same program raised TypeMismatch there -- the same fault-identity
; divergence in a spot the slot bound alone does not reach.

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; slot 0 is in range but unset
LOAD r0          ; so the register is unset and this faults
HALT
